---
description: Backend of the post-discharge patient monitoring platform (research prototype on synthetic data) - FastAPI + SQLite.
import:
  - stdlib/lang/python
---

> Regenerated with turri for the AdaHack 2026 Codeplain challenge. It replaces backend/app of the
> hand-written platform; backend/models/ (the ML models: tracer, camera) is NOT part of this module,
> it is only called. The API contract the React frontend is built against is resources/openapi.json.

***definitions***

- :Api: is the HTTP JSON API of the backend, every path under `/api`, exactly as [the API contract](resources/openapi.json) describes it: paths, methods, operation ids, query parameters and the camelCase field names and types of every request and response body.

- :Today: is the date the backend treats as the current day.
  - It is the date in the environment variable `APP_TODAY` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`) when it is set, otherwise the real current date.

- :Pathway: is a recovery pathway, configured as data: a code, a name, a frequency text, the games its self-check has (each with a game type, a title and its levels) and the daily rating questions.
  - There are exactly two: `stroke` "Možganska kap" and `ctr` "Operacija karpalnega kanala", both with frequency "vsak dan" and the games, in this order, `{"gameType": "trace", "title": "Sledi poti", "levels": [1, 2, 3], "optionalLevels": []}` and `{"gameType": "camera", "title": "Vaje s kamero", "levels": [1, 2, 3], "optionalLevels": [2, 3]}`.
  - An optional level is one the patient may skip.
  - Both ask the same two questions, each with kind "scale", min 1 and max 10: `wellbeing` (text "Kako se počutite danes?", short label "Počutje", min label "Zelo slabo", max label "Odlično", higherIsWorse false) and `pain` (text "Kako močna je bolečina?", short label "Bolečina", min label "Brez bolečine", max label "Zelo močna", higherIsWorse true).

- :Clinician: is a clinician who handles alerts. There is exactly one: id `c1`, name "dr. Ana Novak", role "zdravnica".

- :Patient: is a monitored patient: id, fictional name, birth year, :Pathway: code, affected side (`left` or `right`), discharge date, optional next visit date, whether it is the demo patient, and a sort order.

- :Checkin: is a patient's two daily ratings, `wellbeing` (1-10, higher is better) and `pain` (1-10, higher is worse), for one day, with the time it was made.

- :GameSession: is one played level of a game: patient, game type (`trace` for the tracing game, `camera` for the camera exercises), level, hand, start time, day, duration in ms, whether it was completed, an optional abort reason, the input device (`touch`, `mouse`, `camera`), the score (0-100, none when not scored), the impairment class, the model version, the features (name to number), whether it counts for the trend, the capture quality `qualityOk` (true or false for a camera session the camera scorer judged, null otherwise), and its raw data: the series (name to list of numbers, where a number may be null for a frame without a detection) and the client meta (every key the client sent, also ones not named in the :Api:).

- :ImpairmentClass: of a score is `normal` from 85, `mild` from 65, `moderate` from 40, and `severe` below 40.

- :LevelTrend: is the trend of one patient, one game type and one level as of a day, computed from that level's scored :GameSession: rows that count for the trend, up to and including that day, in order of day, start time and id.
  - The first such session is practice and is left out.
  - The baseline is the median of the next three sessions; there is none until those three exist, and without a baseline the EWMA, delta, delta percent and slope are empty too.
  - The EWMA runs over all sessions after the practice one, with alpha 0.3, seeded with the first of them.
  - The delta is the EWMA minus the baseline; the delta percent is the delta divided by the baseline times 100.
  - The direction is `improving` when the delta is above 5, `declining` below -5, `stable` otherwise, and `insufficient_data` without a baseline.
  - The slope is the least-squares slope, in points per session, of the last 7 scores after the practice one; none with fewer than 3.

- :CombinedTrend: is the trend of one patient and one game type on a day: the mean of the latest delta of every level of that game that has a baseline as of that day, none when no level has one. Its direction follows the same 5-point band as a :LevelTrend:.

- :TrendSnapshot: is a stored row per patient, metric and day: metric `<gameType>:<level>` for a :LevelTrend: and `<gameType>:all` for the :CombinedTrend:, with the number of sessions, baseline, EWMA, slope, delta, delta percent and direction.

- :Alert: is a clinician-facing alert about one patient: source (`game`, `checkin`, `missing`), rule, severity (`red`, `yellow`, `grey`), status (`new`, `acknowledged`, `closed`), a one-sentence Slovenian reason, evidence (a JSON object with a `triggers` list), whether the signals diverge, created and updated times, the day it opened, who acknowledged it and when, who closed it and when, the outcome and a note.

- :Trigger: is one firing of an alert rule as of a day: rule, severity, source, the day of the data it concerns, the reason sentence, the game it concerns (`trace` or `camera`, for the game rules `trend_drop`, `big_drop` and `both`; none for the others), and extra numbers and ids for the evidence.
  - Its key is (rule, game); a stored game-rule trigger without a game is a tracing one, key (rule, `trace`).

- :Games: are the games with their own trend, in this order: `trace` (tracing), then `camera` (camera exercises).

- :GameReason: is the reason sentence of a game rule for the set of games it concerns (written in :Games: order; an empty set counts as tracing alone):
  - `trend_drop`: tracing "Rezultati sledenja so že več dni pod pacientovim izhodiščem."; camera "Rezultati vaj s kamero so že več dni pod pacientovim izhodiščem."; both "Padajo rezultati sledenja in vaj s kamero."
  - `big_drop`: tracing "Rezultati sledenja so močno padli pod pacientovo izhodišče."; camera "Rezultati vaj s kamero so močno padli pod pacientovo izhodišče."; both "Rezultati sledenja in vaj s kamero so močno padli pod pacientovo izhodišče."
  - `both`: tracing "Padajo rezultati sledenja in počutje hkrati."; camera, or tracing and camera, "Padajo rezultati meritev in počutje hkrati."

- :Outcome: is how a clinician closed an :Alert:, one of `called_reassured` "Poklical, pomiril", `adjusted_exercises` "Prilagodil vaje", `visit_moved_earlier` "Pregled prestavljen naprej", `urgent_referral` "Nujna napotitev", `unreachable` "Nedosegljiv", `false_alarm` "Lažni alarm ali težava s podatki".

- :Scorer: is what turns a completed :GameSession: into a score (or none when it cannot be scored), an :ImpairmentClass:, features, a model version and, for a camera session, the capture quality.

- :CameraModels: is the camera exercise code in `<APP_MODELS_DIR>/camera`, used read-only as [the camera bridge](resources/camera_bridge.py) uses it: its module `exercises` (the dict `EXERCISES`, level to exercise) and its module `scoring` (`MODEL_VERSION`, `load_reference()` and `score_camera(game_type, level, hand, duration_ms, series, client_meta, reference=...)`, returning `score`, `impairment_class`, `features`, `model_version`, `quality_ok` and `breakdown`).

- :CameraExercise: is one camera exercise of `EXERCISES`: its level (the dict key; the exercise dicts themselves have no `level` key), `key`, `name`, `detector` (`hand` or `pose`), `duration_s`, `first_cue_s`, `cue_period_s`, `n_cues`, `up_s`, `open_window_s` and `instructions` (a missing key is null).

- :CameraUnavailableVersion: is the model version string `camera-unavailable`.

- :StandinVersion: is the model version string `standin-0.1`.

- :CameraSeed: is the code that gives a seeded camera session plausible features for its score, given in [the camera seed](resources/seed_camera.py).

- :DemoStory: is one of the ten synthetic patient histories the demo is seeded with, given as data and pure functions in [the demo stories](resources/seed_stories.py).

- :CameraPlan: is the camera part of a :DemoStory:'s day k (an active day of the story), exactly as follows.
  - Each story has a camera curve (the base score of camera level 2 on day k, or none: no camera), camera bad days (k to score shift, default none), a camera noise (default 1.5), a camera skip probability (default 0.12) and its camera levels (default 1, 2, 3).
  - For each of its camera levels in order: an optional level (2 or 3) is skipped that day when `rng_for(id, k, "camskip<level>").random()` < the skip probability; otherwise its score is round(clip(curve(k) + bad-day shift + offset + `rng_for(id, k, "cam<level>").gauss(0, noise)`, 4, 100), 1) with offset 2 for level 1, 0 for level 2 and -3 for level 3.
  - `p1`: curve min(94, 84 + 0.35 k).
  - `p2`: curve 86 + 6 (1 - e^(-k/6)); bad days 16: -12, 17: -15, 18: -17, 19: -18, 20: -19, 21: -23 (the arms were badly in the frame); and on day 22 the clinician closes the open alert with outcome `false_alarm` and the note "Pogovor s pacientom: kamera je bila postavljena prenizko, roki nista bili v kadru. Navodila za postavitev ponovljena.".
  - `p3`: curve 88 + 3.5 k / 21 up to day 21, then 91.5 - 0.48 (k - 21); noise 0.6; skip probability 0.
  - `p4`: curve 90 up to day 26, then 90 - 1.9 (k - 26); noise 1.2.
  - `p5`: curve min(94, 83 + 0.4 k).
  - `p6`: curve 90; noise 1.0.
  - `p7`: curve 84 + 0.3 k; camera levels 1 only.
  - `p9`: curve 87; skip probability 0.
  - `p8` and `demo`: no camera curve.

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: uses FastAPI with Pydantic v2, SQLModel on SQLite, and Uvicorn.
  - Runtime dependencies also include numpy, scipy, scikit-learn and joblib, which the external tracer model needs.
- :Implementation: keeps its code in the package `app/`, with `app/main.py` exposing the FastAPI application as `app`.
  - It builds with `uv sync`.
  - It starts with `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT`.
- :Implementation: is laid out as `app/models/` (tables and the Pydantic request and response models), `app/routers/` (one `APIRouter` per resource), `app/services/` (business logic, no HTTP), `app/seed/` (demo data) and `app/db.py` (engine and session).
- :Implementation: declares every request and response body as a Pydantic model with camelCase aliases (`alias_generator=to_camel`, `populate_by_name=True`, `from_attributes=True`), so the JSON matches the :Api: field for field.
  - Datetimes are stored timezone-aware in UTC and serialised as ISO 8601 ending in `Z`; a naive datetime read back from SQLite is treated as UTC.
  - Dates are serialised as `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- :Implementation: answers an error the way FastAPI's `HTTPException` does: the status code and the body `{"detail": "<Slovenian sentence>"}`; request validation failures keep FastAPI's default 422 body.
- :Implementation: reads its settings from environment variables.
  - `APP_DB_URL` is the SQLAlchemy URL of the database, default a SQLite file `data/app.db` in the folder above the package (the folder is created when missing); `sqlite://` is an in-memory database kept on one connection (`StaticPool`, `check_same_thread=False`).
  - `APP_TODAY` sets :Today:.
  - `APP_KEEP_DB` set to `1` makes startup keep an existing database and seed only an empty one; otherwise every startup resets and reseeds the demo.
  - `APP_SEED_HISTORY` set to `0` makes seeding the demo skip the history replay, so it seeds the pathways, the clinician and the patients only; default `1`.
  - `APP_MODELS_DIR` is the folder of the external ML models, default `models` in the folder above the package (in the platform repository that is `backend/models/`).
  - `APP_FRONTEND_DIST` is the built frontend, default `frontend/dist` two folders above the package; when it exists, `/assets` is served from it and every other non-API GET path returns the file at that path or `index.html`.
- :Implementation: gets :Today: and the current time only through one clock module, `app/services/clock.py`, never from `date.today()` or `datetime.now()` elsewhere.
  - The clock can be fixed to a date and shifted by days, which the seed replay and the unit tests use; a reset of the demo clears the shift.
  - "Now" is the real UTC time of day on :Today:.
- :Implementation: writes every :Checkin: and :GameSession: through one ingest service, used by both the :Api: and the seed, so that stored data, trends and alerts always agree.
  - The ingest service takes optional overrides of the day, the creation time and a preset score, which only the seed uses.
- :Implementation: keeps the raw series and client meta of a :GameSession: in a table of their own, keyed by the session id, so listing sessions never loads them.
- :Implementation: stores JSON values (pathway games and questions, check-in answers, session features, series, client meta, alert evidence) in SQLite JSON columns.
- :Implementation: keeps every threshold of the trend, alert, divergence and feedback rules as a named module-level constant.
- :Implementation: loads the external tracer model lazily, at most once per process, as [the tracer bridge](resources/tracer_bridge.py) does, from `<APP_MODELS_DIR>/tracer` (its modules `common`, `features`, `levels` and its artifact `artifacts/tracer_gbm.joblib`), with that folder put on `sys.path`.
  - Any failure to import or call it is logged and makes the :Scorer: use the stand-in.
- :Implementation: loads the :CameraModels: lazily, at most once per process, with `<APP_MODELS_DIR>/camera` appended to `sys.path` (its module `scoring` is imported by that bare name and never shadows the backend's own scoring module), and loads the camera reference once with `load_reference()`.
  - A failure to import them is logged once and leaves the camera exercises unavailable; the backend and the tracing game keep working.
- :Implementation: keeps every client meta key of a session, also ones the :Api: does not name (camera sessions send `videoW`, `videoH`, `fpsMeasured`, `detector` and more), passes them to the :Scorer: and stores them with the raw series.
- :Implementation: keeps a copy of [the tracer levels](resources/tracer_levels.json) as `app/seed/tracer_levels.json` and reads the level paths from it.
- :Implementation: keeps the :DemoStory: data in `app/seed/stories.py` and the :CameraSeed: in `app/seed/camera.py`.
  - `app.services.scoring` provides `camera_duration_s(level)`: the :CameraExercise:'s `duration_s`, or null when unavailable.
- :UnitTests: use FastAPI's `TestClient` and an in-memory SQLite engine per test, with `APP_KEEP_DB=1` and :Today: fixed to 2026-11-21.
- :UnitTests: run with `APP_SEED_HISTORY=0`, except the tests of the history replay, which replay it once per test module and share that database.
  - The whole unit test suite finishes in under 60 seconds.
- :UnitTests: never need `APP_MODELS_DIR` to exist: without the external model the :Scorer: falls back to the stand-in, and without the :CameraModels: camera sessions are stored unscored; tests of the camera bridge stand in for the :CameraModels: with fakes of their own.

***test reqs***

- :ConformanceTests: use pytest and httpx, and run with `pytest`.
- :ConformanceTests: find the built code's folder in the environment variable `BACKEND_BUILD_DIR`.
- :ConformanceTests: start the service from that folder as a separate process with `uv run uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port <free port>`, and wait until `GET /api/meta` answers, for at most 60 seconds.
  - The process gets `APP_TODAY=2026-11-21`, `APP_DB_URL` pointing to a SQLite file in a temporary folder and `APP_MODELS_DIR` set to the folder in the environment variable `BACKEND_MODELS_DIR` (the platform's real ML models).
- :ConformanceTests: read real camera recordings, one JSON file each with `level`, `hand`, `durationMs`, `series` and `clientMeta`, from the folder in the environment variable `CAMERA_RECORDINGS_DIR`, and post them as camera sessions.
  - One service is started for the whole test session; a test that changes data first calls `POST /api/admin/reset`.
- :ConformanceTests: reach the service over HTTP only, never import its code, and stop it when they finish, passing or failing.
- :ConformanceTests: check a failure by its status code, never by its message.
- :ConformanceTests: pass ruff and mypy as the conformance testing script runs them, and are typed throughout.

***functional specs***

# meta-and-pathways
`GET /api/pathways` returns the two :Pathway: rows with their games (each with `gameType`, `title`, `levels` and `optionalLevels`) and questions.

`GET /api/meta` returns :Today:, `syntheticData` true, the list of :Clinician: rows, `outcomes` (each :Outcome: id to its Slovenian label), `modelVersion`, the version of the :Scorer: active now: reading it tries to load the external model if that was not tried yet, and it is the external model's `MODEL_VERSION` when it loaded and its last call did not fail, otherwise :StandinVersion: and `defaultPatientId` `p3`.

# demo-patients
The demo has the two :Pathway: rows, the :Clinician: and the ten :DemoStory: patients (id, name, birth year, pathway, side, sort order, demo flag), each discharged the story's number of days before :Today:, with its next visit the story's number of days after :Today: (none when the story has none).
- `POST /api/admin/reset` drops and recreates every table, clears the clock shift, seeds the demo, and returns `ok` true and the number of patients (10).
- On startup the demo is reset, unless `APP_KEEP_DB=1`, in which case only an empty database is seeded.

# checkins
`POST /api/checkins` with `patientId`, `wellbeing` and `pain` stores a :Checkin: for :Today: and returns its `checkinId`.
- An unknown patient is 404 "Pacient ne obstaja".
- A rating outside 1-10 is 422.
- A second check-in of the same patient on the same day replaces the answers and time of the first one, keeping its id.

# trace-scoring
The :Scorer: scores a `trace` session with the external tracer model when it is available and the level is 1, 2 or 3; otherwise, or when the model fails, with the stand-in.
- The external model is called with level id `line`, `circle` or `maze` for levels 1, 2, 3 and with the coordinate series `targetX`, `targetY`, `x`, `y` multiplied by 1000; its score is clamped to 0-100 and rounded to one decimal, a non-finite score counts as a failure, and an impairment class it returns outside the four is replaced by the :ImpairmentClass: of the score.
- The stand-in takes every k-th point of the trace (k = max(1, points // 300)), the distance of each to the nearest segment of the target polyline, and their mean `mean_dev`; accuracy = max(0, 1 - mean_dev / 0.06), speed = clamp(1 - (duration_s - 8) / 40, 0, 1), score = round(100 * (0.8 * accuracy + 0.2 * speed), 1); features `mean_dev` (4 decimals) and `duration_s` (2 decimals); version :StandinVersion:.
- A trace with fewer than 2 target points or no trace points scores 0, `severe`, no features.
- When the stand-in itself fails (for example on null coordinates), the session is not scorable: no score, no class, no features, :StandinVersion:.

# camera-exercises
`GET /api/camera/exercises` returns every :CameraExercise:, by level, as `level`, `key`, `name`, `detector`, `durationS`, `firstCueS`, `cuePeriodS`, `nCues`, `upS`, `openWindowS` and `instructions`; it returns an empty list when the :CameraModels: are unavailable.

# camera-scoring
The :Scorer: scores a `camera` session with the :CameraModels:: `score_camera("camera", level, hand, duration_ms, series, client_meta, reference=<the loaded reference>)`. There is no stand-in for camera sessions.
- Its features are every finite number in its `features`, plus every finite number in its `breakdown` stored as `part_<key>`; booleans and NaN are left out.
- The capture quality is `bool(quality_ok)`. When the quality is not ok or the score is not a finite number, the session is not scorable: no score and no class, but its features, the capture quality and the model version are kept.
- Otherwise the score is clamped to 0-100 and rounded to 1 decimal; a class outside the four :ImpairmentClass: values is replaced by the class of the score.
- The model version is its `model_version`, or `MODEL_VERSION` of the camera `scoring` module.
- When `score_camera` raises, the session is not scorable, with no features and that version; when the :CameraModels: are unavailable, it is not scorable with no features and :CameraUnavailableVersion:.

# sessions
`POST /api/sessions` takes a game result (`patientId`, `gameType` `trace` or `camera`, `level`, `hand`, `startedAt`, `durationMs` >= 0, `completed`, `abortReason`, `series` whose values are lists of numbers or nulls, `clientMeta` with `inputDevice`, `canvasW`, `canvasH`, `devicePixelRatio`, `userAgent` and any further keys), stores a :GameSession: for :Today: and returns `sessionId` and `scored`.
- An unknown patient is 404 "Pacient ne obstaja"; a level that is not one of its game's levels in the :Pathway: games (1, 2, 3 for both games) is 422 "Neznana stopnja igre"; another game type is 422.
- A completed session is scored by the :Scorer:. It is scored, and counts for the trend, only when the :Scorer: gave a score and the capture quality is not false; otherwise it is stored without score and class, does not count for the trend, and `scored` is false, but keeps the model version, features and capture quality the :Scorer: gave.
- An aborted session is not scored: no score, class, model version, features or capture quality; it does not count for the trend and `scored` is false.
- Repeated sessions of the same level on the same day are all stored and all count.

`GET /api/sessions/{sessionId}/raw` returns the session's id, patient, game type, level, day, score, series (with its nulls) and client meta (every key that was sent); an unknown id is 404 "Seja ne obstaja".

# trend-snapshots
After a scored :GameSession: is stored, the :TrendSnapshot: rows of that patient, game type and day are recomputed and upserted. Every game has its own trends: tracing (`trace`) and camera (`camera`) histories never mix.
- There is one `<gameType>:<level>` row for every level played that day, holding that level's :LevelTrend: and its number of sessions.
- There is one `<gameType>:all` row holding the :CombinedTrend: (baseline, EWMA, slope and delta percent empty), whose number of sessions is the number of distinct days with a scored session so far. A level not played that day contributes its latest delta, so a self-check still in progress never shows one level as the whole trend.

# divergence
The divergence of a patient as of a day compares, for each of the :Games:, the delta of its latest `<game>:all` snapshot up to that day (a game whose latest snapshot has an empty delta, or that has none, is left out) with the change of the patient's wellbeing index. A patient without camera data is judged on tracing alone.
- The wellbeing index of a :Checkin: is the mean of its answered ratings normalised to 0-1 by each question's range, inverted for a question where higher is worse.
- The change is the mean index of the last 7 days (day - 6 to day) minus the mean of the 7 days before; there is none when either week has no check-in.
- It diverges when any game's delta is at most -10 and the change is at least -0.05, with the sentence "Rezultati sledenja padajo, pacient pa poroča enako ali boljše počutje." when tracing is the only such game, otherwise "Rezultati meritev padajo, pacient pa poroča enako ali boljše počutje.".
- Else it diverges when every game's |delta| is below 5 and the change is at most -0.15, with "Rezultati sledenja so stabilni, pacient pa poroča slabše počutje." when tracing is the only game with a delta, otherwise "Rezultati meritev so stabilni, pacient pa poroča slabše počutje.".
- Otherwise, or without any game delta or without a change, it does not diverge and has no sentence.

# alert-rules
As of a day, these :Trigger: rules are evaluated for a patient (reasons word for word).
- `trend_drop`, yellow, source game, for each of the :Games: on its own: the latest `<game>:all` snapshot with a delta has delta <= -10, and at least 2 of the up to 3 snapshots of that game with a delta before it have delta <= -5. Its game is that game, its reason the :GameReason: of that game alone; extra `delta` (1 decimal), `sessionIds` (the counting sessions of that game on those snapshot days) and `previousDeltas` (1 decimal).
- `big_drop`, red, source game, for each of the :Games: on its own: that game's latest delta <= -20. Its game is that game, its reason the :GameReason: of that game alone; extra `delta` and `sessionIds`.
- `subjective_drop`, yellow, source checkin: per rating, the mean of the check-ins of the recent week (day - 6 to day) minus the mean of the week before (day - 13 to day - 7), with at least 2 check-ins in each week; it fires when wellbeing fell by at least 2 or pain rose by at least 2. Its day is the last recent check-in's day; reason "Pacient poroča slabše počutje kot prejšnji teden.", "Pacient poroča močnejšo bolečino kot prejšnji teden." or, both, "Pacient poroča slabše počutje in močnejšo bolečino kot prejšnji teden."; extra `wellbeingChange` and `painChange` (2 decimals or null) and `checkinIds` of the recent week.
- `both`, red, source game: one for each game whose `trend_drop` holds while `subjective_drop` holds; its game is that game, its day the later of the two, its reason the :GameReason: of that game alone; extra that game's `delta`, `wellbeingChange`, `painChange`.
- The triggers of one evaluation come in the order: the `both` triggers, the `big_drop` triggers, the `trend_drop` triggers (each group worst game first, by its delta, lowest first), then `subjective_drop`.

# alert-merging
Evaluating the alerts of a patient as of a day, after every ingested :Checkin: or :GameSession:, keeps at most one open (not closed) :Alert: per patient.
- A trigger is suppressed when a clinician-closed alert of the patient (not one closed by `system`) has a trigger with the same :Trigger: key (rule and game; an alert without stored triggers has its own rule as key), the trigger is not more severe than that alert, and either the trigger's day is on or before the closing day or the closing was less than 7 days before the evaluated day.
- Without an open alert, the live triggers open a new one with status `new`, opened on the day, taking source, rule, severity and reason from the most severe trigger; at equal severity `both` beats `big_drop`, which beats the rest.
- With an open alert, triggers whose (rule, game, day) it already lists are not appended again; a more severe or higher-priority trigger replaces its source, rule, severity and reason, and when it is more severe and the alert was `acknowledged`, the alert returns to `new` with the acknowledgement cleared.
- Every appended trigger is listed in `evidence.triggers` as `{rule, severity, source, day, reason}`, plus `game` when it has one; `sessionIds` and `checkinIds` in the evidence are the sorted union of all live triggers'; `wellbeingChange`, `painChange` and `missedDays` take the latest value.
- When the live triggers include game-rule triggers, the evidence gets `games`, `delta` and `previousDeltas` from them: `games` is, in :Games: order, `{<game>: {"delta": <its delta>}}` for every game with a live game-rule trigger (it replaces the stored `games`, so a game that recovered drops out); `delta` is the lowest of those deltas; `previousDeltas` are that worst game's `trend_drop` previous deltas when it has a live one (otherwise the stored value stays). Without live game-rule triggers these three keep their stored values. On every evaluation, also one that appends no trigger, these are merged into the stored evidence: `sessionIds` and `checkinIds` become the sorted union of the ids already stored and those of the live triggers; a number is overwritten only by a live trigger that has it (a non-null value wins over null); keys no live trigger has keep their stored value.
- The triggers of one evaluation are considered, and appended, in the order the rules give them.
- The reason of an open alert whose rule is a game rule is the :GameReason: of its rule for every game that has a game-rule trigger in its `evidence.triggers`; it is updated whenever that changes.
- The alert's `diverging` flag follows the patient's divergence as of the day, and `evidence.divergence` holds its sentence; the key is written only when the sentence differs from the stored one (a missing key counts as null), so an alert that never diverged has no `divergence` key.
- The created time, and the updated time whenever triggers are appended, are "now" when the day is :Today:, otherwise noon UTC of that day; an evaluation that appends nothing leaves the updated time as it is.

# missing-data-alerts
A grey `no_data` alert (source missing, reason "Pacient že več dni nima nobenega vnosa ali meritve.", extra `missedDays`) opens for a patient without an open alert when the discharge was at least 4 days ago and at least 4 days have passed since the latest of their last check-in day, last session day and discharge date.
- A sweep over all patients does this as of a day; it runs when the patient list is read and during the seed. The sweep only closes grey alerts that new data answered and opens grey ones; it never evaluates the game or check-in rules and never changes another alert's evidence.
- An open grey `no_data` alert closes by itself, closed by `system` with no outcome, as soon as the patient has a check-in or a session on or after its opening day, unless a live yellow or red trigger escalates it instead.

# alert-api
`GET /api/alerts?status=open|closed|all` (default `open`) lists alerts by id, highest first, each with its patient's name.

`POST /api/alerts/{alertId}/ack` with `clinicianId`, `close` (default false), `outcome` and `note` acknowledges an alert and optionally closes it, returning the alert.
- An unknown alert is 404 "Opozorilo ne obstaja"; an unknown clinician is 404 "Zdravnik ne obstaja".
- Closing without an outcome is 422 "Opozorila ni mogoče zapreti brez izbranega izida."; an alert already closed is 422 "Opozorilo je že zaprto.".
- The first acknowledgement records the clinician's name and the time, and a `new` alert becomes `acknowledged`; closing sets status `closed`, the closer's name, the time and the outcome; a given note is stored; the updated time is always set.

# patient-list
`GET /api/patients` first runs the missing-data sweep as of :Today:, then returns :Today:, the triage counters and every patient, sorted by urgency (red, yellow, no_data, insufficient_data, stable), then newest open alert first, then sort order.
- A patient with an open alert has the status of its severity (`no_data` for grey) and its reason; a grey one's reason is "Brez vnosa že N dni." counting to :Today:.
- Status, reason and the detail summary are about tracing. Otherwise N days without any entry (since the last entry, or the discharge), N >= 4, is `no_data` "Brez vnosa že N dni."; without a `trace:all` snapshot it is `insufficient_data` "Premalo sej za izhodišče (n od 4)." where n is the largest number of completed counting trace sessions of one trace level, at most 3; else `stable` with "Rezultati so nad izhodiščem." (improving), "Rezultati so nekoliko pod izhodiščem." (declining) or "Brez posebnosti; rezultati so blizu izhodišča.".
- Each item has days since discharge, days to the next visit, the open alert id, diverging (the open alert's flag, otherwise the divergence as of :Today:), the game sparkline `gameSparkline` (day and delta of the last 21 `trace:all` snapshots with a delta), the camera sparkline `cameraSparkline` (the same for `camera:all`, empty without camera data) and the wellbeing sparkline (day and wellbeing of the last 21 check-ins).
- Counters: `needsAttention` is red + yellow, `noData` is no_data, `stable` is stable + insufficient_data, `total` is all.

# patient-detail
`GET /api/patients/{patientId}` returns the patient with their :Pathway:, dates, days since discharge and to the next visit, status, reason and diverging as in the patient list, the open alert, and a summary: number of sessions and check-ins, last session and check-in days, and the latest `trace:all` delta and direction (`insufficient_data` when none). An unknown patient is 404 "Pacient ne obstaja" on every patient path.

`GET /api/patients/{patientId}/timeline` returns :Today:, the discharge and next visit dates, all sessions (without raw data, each with its `qualityOk`) by start time, all check-ins by day, all trend snapshots by day and all alerts by id, closed ones included.

# patient-home
`GET /api/patients/{patientId}/home` returns exactly the fields `patientId`, `name`, `pathwayCode`, `pathwayName`, `hand` (the affected side), `today` (:Today:), `steps`, `selfcheckDoneToday` (the ratings and every non-camera step done; camera steps never block it: no camera, no permission and skipped exercises are all fine) and `lastSelfcheckDay` (the last day up to :Today: with a check-in or a session, or null).
- Each step has exactly `id`, `kind`, `title`, `gameType`, `level`, `done`, `skippable` and `durationS`. The steps are, in order, `ratings` (kind `ratings`, title "Počutje in bolečina", `gameType` and `level` null, not skippable, no duration, done when there is a check-in today) and one step per game level of the pathway, games in their order, with id `<gameType>:<level>`, kind `game`, its `gameType` and `level`, title "Ravna črta", "Krog", "Labirint" for trace levels 1-3 and "Dlan", "Roke v stran", "Dvig rok" for camera levels 1-3 (else "Stopnja N"), `skippable` when the level is one of its game's optional levels, `durationS` the :CameraExercise:'s `duration_s` for a camera step (null when unavailable) and null for a trace step, done when a completed session of that game and level exists today.

# patient-feedback
Patient feedback as of a day uses, for each of the :Games:, its `<game>:all` snapshots with a delta up to that day, oldest first; every game weighs the same and their scores never mix; it never shows a number.
- Without any snapshot of any game: tone `first`, trend `unknown`.
- The described day is the latest day that any game has a snapshot on. For every game whose latest snapshot is on the described day, its difference is its latest delta minus the mean of its up to 5 deltas before it (0 when none). The tone is decided by the mean of those differences: `better` at >= 3, `lower` at <= -3, else `similar`.
- A game's trend: `declining` when the patient's open yellow or red alert has a game-rule trigger of that game (a game-rule trigger without a game counting as tracing); else, comparing its latest delta with its delta 5 session-days earlier (or its first), `declining` when latest <= -5 and at least 3 lower, `improving` when latest >= 5 and at least 3 higher, else `stable`.
- The overall trend is `declining` when any game is declining, else `improving` when any game is improving, else `stable`.
- Title and text come from [the feedback messages](resources/feedback_messages.md) by (tone, trend); `first` or `unknown` always gives the first-day message.

Each game also has its own progress, `games`: one entry per game with at least one `<gameType>:all` snapshot with a delta up to :Today:, tracing first, each exactly `gameType`, `title` ("Sledenje" for trace, "Vaje s kamero" for camera), `trend` (that game's trend), `points` and `personalBestDay` (the day of its highest delta over the whole history, ties to the later day).

`GET /api/patients/{patientId}/selfcheck/summary` returns exactly `tone`, `trend`, `title`, `text` (the feedback for :Today:, flat, not nested), `patientId`, `day` (:Today:), `levelsDone` (game steps of all games done today), `levelsTotal` (game steps in total) and `games` (the same full entries as `games` of the progress, each with exactly `gameType`, `title`, `trend`, `points` and `personalBestDay`, except that `points` holds only the points of the last 14 days, :Today: included).

`GET /api/patients/{patientId}/progress` returns exactly `tone`, `trend`, `title`, `text` (flat), `patientId`, `games` (each with all its points), `ratings` (each check-in up to :Today: as `day`, `wellbeing`, `pain`), `weekDone` (days with any entry in the last 7 days), `weekGoal` (5) and `clinicianReviewedAt` (the latest acknowledgement time of any of the patient's alerts, or null).
- A point has exactly `day`, `value` (its delta rounded to 1 decimal) and `label`: `lower` at <= -5, `better` at >= 5, else `usual`.

# demo-history
Seeding the demo also replays each :DemoStory:'s history, day by day, from the day after the earliest discharge up to yesterday.
- With :Today: fixed to the replayed day, each story's plan of day k (days since discharge, k >= 1) is written through the ingest service: first the check-in at hour h-1, minute 30, then one completed trace session per level at hour h, minute 5 x level, where h = 8 + (sum of the character codes of the patient id) mod 9. Then the missing-data sweep runs, then the story's clinician actions of day k are applied to the patient's open alert as clinician `c1`. Today itself only gets the sweep.
- A session's score is preset from the story (version :StandinVersion:, class by :ImpairmentClass:); its features are `level_features(level, score, rng_for(id, k, "feat<level>"))` and its trace `synthetic_trace(level, mean_dev * 1.4, duration_ms=int(duration_s * 1000), lifts=int(lifts), seed="<id>:<k>:<level>")` from [the trace generator](resources/seed_traces.py), with the stored features `dev_mean` (mean_dev / 0.06, 3 decimals), `duration_s`, `n_pauses` (round(pause_rate_hz x duration_s / 4)) and `n_lifts`.
- The client meta is `touch` 360x360 at pixel ratio 3 or `mouse` 480x480 at pixel ratio 2, with user agent "seed (touch)" or "seed (mouse)", by the story's input device.
- After the trace sessions of day k come the story's camera sessions (none for a story without a camera curve), by the :CameraPlan:, in level order: one completed camera session per level at hour h, minute 20 + 4 x level, with duration the :CameraExercise:'s `duration_s` x 1000 (30000 when unavailable) and an empty series, since nothing was recorded.
  - Its score is preset from the story with model version `camera-seed`, class by :ImpairmentClass:, capture quality true, and the features of the :CameraSeed:: `features(level, score, rng_for(id, k, "camfeat<level>"))`.
  - Its client meta is `camera` 1280x720 at pixel ratio 1, user agent "seed (camera)", plus `videoW` 1280, `videoH` 720 and `fpsMeasured` the features' `fps`.
